			<div class="content" id="post-content-2282322">
									

<p>I mentioned it in my post but no, diamond tipped bullets are far from practical. For one, they'd be very expensive, and would cause extensive damage to any gun using them in a short period of time. Even though a diamond tipped bullet is hard, it'd either shatter at contact, or just bounce off the intended target due to diamond's low density.</p>
<p>I guess the use of diamond in cutting tools misled the author. Diamond dust leftover from diamond cutting is used on diamond-tipped saws, since the cutting tool only needs hardness, not density.</p>

